###################################################
# Data loading from DB

## Purpose
  load data from DB for block list and other features.
  Update the BlockListRobot.json and POI.json and start_motion.json if there are data changes in the DB.
  This function is triggered by the button, 'Update Blocks'

## Conditions
  DB connection parameters are set in dbinfo.json.
  Create DB library for CRUD with sql query. It should be a different file.
  Use DB library load data for block list from the table
  Update only the data scopes specified below, 'Block list' part.
  Do not update unrelated categories/items.
  Before writing DB values, remove only the existing values that belong to the same DB-managed scope.
  Keep all non-targeted existing values as-is.
  If target table has no rows or no applicable data, keep current values for that target scope.

## Block list
  - category: motion
    action: 'motion/start_motion'
      target: parameters[].task_type.options[].value: 'expressive_motion'
        DB info for parameters:
          Table: MotionExpressive
          Columns
            value: name
            description: description
      target: parameters[].task_type.options[].value: 'pose_motion'
        DB info for parameters:
          Table: MotionPose
          Columns
            value: name
            description: description
    action: 'BRIC.start_motion:motion/start_motion'
      target: parameters[].name: 'name'
        DB info for parameters:
          Table: MotionExpressive
          Columns for key
            value: name
            description: description
          format:
            name: 'expressive_motion.{value}'
      target: parameters[].name: 'name'
        DB info for parameters:
          Table: MotionPose
          Columns for key
            value: name
            description: description
          format:
            name: 'pose_motion.{value}'
      merge/update rule:
        - Remove only existing `expressive_motion.*` values when `MotionExpressive` has rows.
        - Remove only existing `pose_motion.*` values when `MotionPose` has rows.
        - Keep other existing values (e.g., manipulation) unchanged.
